WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.238
On plastics press twelve, the
melt temperature begins to rise.

00:00:04.608 --> 00:00:06.804
An individual cycle can look ordinary.

00:00:06.804 --> 00:00:09.105
It is the movement
across successive cycles

00:00:09.105 --> 00:00:11.196
that tells the setter where to look.

00:00:11.906 --> 00:00:16.659
On an unconnected press, VP Expert
starts when the operator sees a defect.

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:21.679
On a connected press, VP Predict compares
measurements as they arrive. Here,

00:00:21.679 --> 00:00:24.275
the drift and the phone
alert are simulated.

00:00:24.985 --> 00:00:27.620
Select melt temperature
and choose an upward drift.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.311
The simulator establishes a
reference during stable running.

00:00:31.311 --> 00:00:32.972
Each new point is one cycle.

00:00:32.972 --> 00:00:36.344
Normal variation and a persistent
trend are different things.

00:00:37.055 --> 00:00:39.972
Watch the smoothed trend
move away from its reference.

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:44.047
An alert can be raised before the measured
value crosses the tolerance limit.

00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:48.591
That does not mean the part has failed.
It is a reason to inspect the process.

00:00:49.301 --> 00:00:51.843
The phone identifies the
press and the signal.

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:54.181
The setter acknowledges
the alert and decides

00:00:54.181 --> 00:00:56.468
how to handle the press during diagnosis.

00:00:56.838 --> 00:00:59.501
If no one responds, the
demonstration describes

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.902
a simulated escalation to the team leader.

00:01:02.612 --> 00:01:05.562
VP Expert takes over. In
this plastics example,

00:01:05.562 --> 00:01:09.495
check whether the temperature
setpoint was changed without a record.

00:01:09.865 --> 00:01:12.424
The ranking is a guide, not a probability.

00:01:12.424 --> 00:01:15.661
Test one authorised action and
watch the following cycles.

00:01:16.371 --> 00:01:19.584
Confirm whether the signal has
returned to its reference zone.

00:01:19.584 --> 00:01:23.139
Record the drift, the cause
checked, the action and the result.

00:01:23.509 --> 00:01:25.721
The demonstration history is temporary.

00:01:25.721 --> 00:01:28.809
Here it illustrates what a
reviewed case should contain.

00:01:29.519 --> 00:01:33.557
VP Predict adds cycle monitoring to
VP Expert on connectable presses.

00:01:33.557 --> 00:01:37.706
An alert starts an investigation;
it does not approve an adjustment.
